<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-12163] .NET: CacheEntryEventType.Removed is not being risen</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-12163</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Steps to reproduce:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Create a cache with user-defined type&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Add an ICacheEntryEventListener in order to be notified of CacheEntryEventType.Removed events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Put a value in the cache&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Remove that value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Expected: CacheEntryEventType.Removed event get captured&lt;br/&gt;
Actual: CacheEntryEventType.Updated event get captured&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Update:&lt;br/&gt;
After these changes &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-8714&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-8714&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
New logic of detecting events (ContinuousQueryUtils.cs) now relies on the Object.Equals method which is not intuitive at all.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
